WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.360
After eight seasons of build-up, the namesake
"mother" on CBS's How I Met Your Mother was

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:06.810
finally revealed in 2013.

00:00:06.810 --> 00:00:11.730
It was one of the most anticipated moments
in TV history, so the absolute perfect actress

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:12.730
had to be cast.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.000
The producers somehow found the right woman
for the job: a then little-known actress named

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.119
Cristin Milioti.

00:00:18.119 --> 00:00:22.530
Here's what else she's appeared in, both before
and after How I Met Your Mother.

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:23.530
Once (Broadway)

00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.810
Fans of the New York theater scene may recognize
Milioti from her stage work.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.220
She's performed steadily both on and off Broadway
for more than a decade.

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:36.350
Most notably, when the 2007 indie hit Once
was adapted for the theater in 2011 theater,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:41.000
Milioti played the unnamed female lead, earning
a Tony Award nomination for Best Performance

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.490
by a Leading Actress in a Musical.

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:44.969
The Sopranos

00:00:44.969 --> 00:00:49.190
While pursuing a career as a stage actor in
New York, Milioti landed roles in some TV

00:00:49.190 --> 00:00:52.970
productions based out of the Tri-State area,
including The Sopranos.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:57.730
Toward the end of the HBO mob drama's run,
Milioti played Catherine Sacrimoni, daughter

00:00:57.730 --> 00:01:02.269
of John Sacrimoni, the ruthless boss of the
Lupertazzi crime family.

00:01:02.269 --> 00:01:04.540
"You're the one that wanted a big wedding!"

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.020
"Catherine, your sister has enough to deal
with without the commentary."

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:09.340
30 Rock

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:13.540
Another New York-based TV show that hired
Milioti was NBC's 30 Rock.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:19.020
In 2011, Milioti portrayed a seemingly shallow
standup comedian named Abby Flynn who affects

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.340
a so-called "sexy baby" voice.

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:26.780
Tina Fey's Liz Lemon hires her to be a writer
for TGS with Tracy Jordan after a blog accuses

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.720
the sketch comedy show of being misogynistic.

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.760
"Lemon, is that the new woman you hired?"

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:38.180
"Is it cold in here, or is it just that I'm
not wearing any underwear?"

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:43.680
Milioti has to do some high-wire comic acting—as
it turns out, the Abby Flynn act is a ruse;

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:48.500
she's really a comedian named Abby Grossman
hiding from a crazed ex-husband.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.310
Sleepwalk With Me

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.940
Stand-up comedian, actor, and writer Mike
Birbiglia has presented Sleepwalk With Me

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:57.820
as a one-man show, a book, and, in 2012, a
feature film.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:02.780
In the largely autobiographical dramedy about
the comedian's history of severe sleep disorders,

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:07.900
along with his anxieties over his career and
romantic life, Milioti portrayed Janet Pandamiglio,

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:09.440
Birbiglia's sister.

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.250
The film was a critical hit and played well
on the festival circuit, winning an Audience

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:15.629
Award at the Sundance Film Festival.

00:02:15.629 --> 00:02:17.310
The Wolf of Wall Street

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:22.040
Milioti became a full-time cast member of
How I Met Your Mother in the fall of 2013,

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.230
right around the same time as the release
of The Wolf of Wall Street, a darkly comic

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:31.090
biopic about the rise and fall of disgraced
stockbroker Jordan Belfort, played by Leonardo

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.090
DiCaprio.

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:36.959
Milioti portrayed Teresa, Jordan's sweet and
patient first wife, later abandoned for a

00:02:36.959 --> 00:02:39.290
blonde bombshell played by Margot Robbie.

00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.459
The Garden State native is 100% New Jersey
in the role, with an accent as big and bold

00:02:44.459 --> 00:02:46.319
as her 1980s hair.

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:47.319
A to Z

00:02:47.319 --> 00:02:52.019
Unfortunately, the very nature of her role
on How I Met Your Mother meant Milioti was

00:02:52.019 --> 00:02:54.330
out of work after the show's final season.

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:58.670
But by fall 2014, Milioti was already starring
in another network sitcom.

00:02:58.670 --> 00:03:02.849
Something of a successor to How I Met Your
Mother with its rom-com sensibility and slow-build

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:07.489
storyline, NBC's A to Z aimed to tell the
complete story of a relationship from the

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:10.840
"meet cute" to the "happily ever after" … or
the split.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.489
Ben Feldman of Mad Men portrayed Andrew opposite
Milioti's Zelda.

00:03:14.489 --> 00:03:18.200
Despite some critical praise for the show
and the cast, the series didn't attract much

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:23.010
of an audience, and NBC broke up with A to
Z after 13 episodes.

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.340
Fargo

00:03:24.340 --> 00:03:29.040
Milioti popped up in a small but pivotal role
in the second season of FX's Fargo.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.769
Milioti's character is dying of cancer, and
her appearance heartbreakingly links the second

00:03:33.769 --> 00:03:36.219
season of the series with the first.

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:41.340
In the '70s-set second season, Milioti plays
Betsy Solverson, wife of state trooper Lou.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:45.489
Their daughter, Molly grows up to become a
cop, too… as played by Allison Tolman in

00:03:45.489 --> 00:03:48.340
the 2006-set first season.

00:03:48.340 --> 00:03:49.909
The Mindy Project

00:03:49.909 --> 00:03:53.900
In 2015, Milioti scored a recurring role on
The Mindy Project.

00:03:53.900 --> 00:03:57.730
She played Whitney, a tough-as-nails, workaholic
hedge fund manager.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:01.750
Milioti's character appeared in five episodes,
dating one of the doctors in the sitcom's

00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:06.010
central medical practice and also becoming
a new, if brief, best friend for Mindy.

00:04:06.010 --> 00:04:11.000
Whitney is a financial genius who helps the
scatterbrained Mindy get her finances in order.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:15.279
It also turns out that Whitney's a recovering
cocaine addict, giving Milioti a chance to

00:04:15.279 --> 00:04:17.280
do some dark-yet-wacky comedy.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:19.060
"Why don't we hang out tonight.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.060
How's 9?"

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:25.180
"Five works better for me given my situation
and because 5:10 is the 4:20 of cocaine."

00:04:25.180 --> 00:04:26.720
"Oh yeah, of course"

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:27.820
Thanks for watching!

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:30.290
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.360
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

